From 35a6d6df26a8d9c5743d23c3fe954198b1de4d56 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wang lian <lianux.mm@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 11 Jun 2026 15:42:39 +0800
Subject: [RFC PATCH 6/8] mm/damon: add SPE feedback prototype for sub-THP
 split decisions

Introduce a CONFIG_DAMON_SPE prototype that provides sub-THP access
heatmap data to DAMOS_MTHP_SPLIT, enabling intelligent split decisions
based on access patterns within THPs.

The prototype uses PTE access bits via folio_walk for THPs that have
been previously split to PTEs.  For PMD-mapped THPs (the common case),
it returns -EOPNOTSUPP and the split handler falls back to unconditional
split.  This mirrors the behavior gap that ARM SPE fills: SPE samples
provide per-subpage access data without requiring the PMD to be split
first.

Architecture:
  mm/damon/spe.h        - Interface: damon_spe_folio_heatmap(),
                          damon_spe_hot_fraction()
  mm/damon/spe.c        - Prototype implementation using PTE access bits
  mm/damon/vaddr.c      - Integration: skip split if THP is >80% hot

Production path (Kunpeng 920+):
  Replace the PTE-walk implementation with ARM SPE PMU buffer reading
  via perf_event_create_kernel_counter(), decoding SPE records to
  extract {virt_addr, phys_addr, access_type}, and aggregating into
  a per-process access heatmap.

Co-developed-by: Kunwu Chan <kunwu.chan@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Kunwu Chan <kunwu.chan@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Wang Lian <lianux.mm@gmail.com>
